1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,120
In this video we shall review how to handle false positives in BurpSuite Enterprise Edition.

2
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:14,520
You may want to do this if manual testing shows that an issue is not really present,

3
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:21,180
or if you are aware of the issue but do not want to rectify it. To mark an issue as a false positive,

4
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:28,480
first from the top menu select scans. Then select the scan that you wish to view. Next,

5
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:39,160
click the issues tab and locate the vulnerability in question. Now you can select mark as false positive.

6
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:46,120
In the pop-up window select a reason. You can select this issue to mark only this instance of

7
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:51,880
the issue as a false positive. You can select this issue and all existing issues with the same type

8
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:58,120
for the site. This marks all issues of the same type as false positives across the whole site.

9
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:06,820
Or we can select this issue and all existing issues with the same type and URL for the site. This marks

10
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:13,360
issues of the same type and URL as false positives. Finally, we can select all issues of this type in

11
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:20,140
the current scan only. This marks all issues of this type as false positives but only for the current scan.

12
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:28,840
Finally, select OK. In the issues window, the selected issues are now moved to the bottom of the list,

13
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:36,580
labelled as false positive. They are also greyed out. They will be removed from stats and charts displayed

14
00:01:36,580 --> 00:01:45,940
in the dashboard. Please note marking an issue as false positive does not affect future scans. To configure

15
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:51,220
future scans to mark certain issues by default, refer to configuring default false positive settings

16
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:53,680
documentation. Thank you.

